# Claude Code (2.1.295 and later). It is not open source; its states are as other terminals
# document them (Kaku's docs/agent-skill.md: working, blocked, done, error, idle over OSC 7501).
# The app value and messages here are **unconfirmed** - `claude-code` is the protocol's own
# example (docs:program-status, Keys) - until a real session is captured with
# tools/agent-status-capture and added as its own fixture. Root record only, as a single agent.

report state=idle:app=claude-code
expect none
report state=working:app=claude-code
expect running
report state=blocked:kind=permission:app=claude-code | msg=Bash(npm test)
expect needs-you
report state=working:app=claude-code
expect running
report state=done:app=claude-code
expect needs-you
report state=working:app=claude-code
expect running
report state=blocked:kind=question:app=claude-code | msg=Which file?
expect needs-you
report state=working:app=claude-code
expect running
report state=done:app=claude-code
expect needs-you
see
expect none
report state=idle:app=claude-code
expect none
